.Dd November 20, 2026
.Dt ZPOOL-RELOCATE 8
.Os
.
.Sh NAME
.Nm zpool-relocate
.Nd relocate eligible file blocks from a special vdev
.
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm zpool
.Cm relocate
.Op Fl b Ar bytes
.Op Fl c Ar cursor
.Ar pool Ar vdev
.
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Relocate a batch of file blocks from a top-level special vdev to the normal
allocation class while the pool is online.
The pool must have the
.Sy brt_relocation
feature enabled.
The command supports file and volume data and metadata with equal source
and destination allocation sizes.
Each distinct block is moved once, including blocks shared by snapshots or
block clones.
.Pp
Blocks whose source and destination allocation sizes differ are skipped.
The command prints the number of relocated blocks, bytes, skipped blocks and
visited pointers, a completion flag, an error number, and a cursor.
Pass the cursor to the next invocation to continue the same pass.
The first invocation fixes the upper birth TXG of the pass.
Start a new pass to consider later allocations.
A completed pass makes the released space available to the pool.
Use
.Xr zpool-remove 8
to remove the device and copy its remaining allocations.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl b Ar bytes
Limit the total allocation size moved by this invocation.
The default is 1 MiB.
.It Fl c Ar cursor
Continue a pass using the cursor printed by an earlier invocation.
.El
.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr zpool-features 7 ,
.Xr zpool-remove 8
